{{ comp.hero({
  tagline: "Define the public boundary once. NetScript carries it through the stack.",
  subhead: "NetScript is a meta-framework for Deno. It composes Fresh, Hono, oRPC, and Aspire into one workspace. A database-backed shape can flow from a generated model schema into a versioned contract, through the service, to the rendered page, and the whole system runs as one observed resource graph.",
  ctas: [
    { label: "Start a workspace", href: "/quickstart/", primary: true },
    { label: "Why NetScript", href: "/why/" }
  ]
}) }}

<p class="ns-lede">
Frameworks supply the web layer, the service layer, or the orchestrator, and leave the boundaries
between them to the application. At those boundaries, request types diverge, durable work shrinks
to a local retry loop, and incident evidence splits across logs, resource state, and traces.
NetScript gives each operation one versioned public contract. It types the handler and the client
from that contract and generates the OpenAPI description from it, so nothing derived from the
contract can drift from it. The contract narrows or extends a generated model schema when one
exists; otherwise you write it directly.
</p>

